These statistics are NOT 100% accurate, but they likely are as realistic as (reasonably) possible.

??? info "How This Is Calculated"

    The definition of an entry (or a "complete" torrent) is quite murky.
    SeaDex defines it as an AniList entry, but every private tracker has their own definition
    (typically, they follow AniDB or TVDB), while Nyaa does not enforce a specific definition.
    Every release can quite possibly have slightly different torrents across trackers,
    or a single torrent on Nyaa can include several SeaDex entries.
    A Nyaa torrent might contain an entire franchise, but only a single file out of it might be relevant.

    All of this and more means that we need to settle on a method to calculate these statistics.
    For each SeaDex entry and exact group name, private tracker torrents are preferred:
    if any exist, only those are considered; otherwise, all of the group's public torrents are considered.
    Exact duplicate torrent records are discarded across entries before summing their file sizes.
    Group names are not normalized.

    The entry count records how many times a group appears across entries,
    with each group counted up to twice per entry—once for best torrents and once for alt torrents.
    This avoids skewing counts from entries with multiple torrents
    (e.g., a group with 12 single-episode alt torrents counts as one alt entry).
    Counts include both statuses even when the private-tracker preference removes their public torrents from size calculations.

    The realistic size estimates downloading one preferred release per entry.
    It first considers the best dual-audio torrent on a private tracker, then best dual-audio torrent on any tracker,
    then the best torrent on a private tracker, then best torrent on any tracker, and finally any available release.
    The first torrent in SeaDex's order within that preference is selected, and exact duplicate records count once.

    The average is the total size divided by the entry count, rather than the number of torrents.

